 "final_text_tail": "normalize_image` and in `_get_image_id_bytes`, so the failure most likely escapes from the image loading path in `ImageMediaIO.load_bytes`. That method only converts `OSError`, `UnidentifiedImageError` and `SyntaxError` into client errors, so any other exception it raises becomes a server error. I haven't confirmed which exception a broken EXIF block triggers.\n\n{\"files\": [\"vllm/multimodal/media/image.py\", \"vllm/multimodal/image.py\", \"vllm/multimodal/hasher.py\"], \"functions\": [\"ImageMediaIO.load_bytes\", \"normalize_image\", \"_get_image_id_bytes\", \"open_image\", \"ImageMediaIO._convert_image_mode\"]}",
